Z||000005||ChadMan||09-24-1999||09:22 AM||||The 88 brakes are amazingly better than the 84-87 - the pedal feel is much firmer and they don't fade much, if at all.  The handling is better on the 88's, too, but not drastically better than a properly aligned 84-87.  Suspension and brake parts are marginally more expensive for the 88's, too.  <P>From all I've heard and read, all the engine swaps you can do with the 84-87 can also be done with the 88, including the Buick 3800 V6.  I bought my 88 Coupe with the thought that I'd swap in a Buick 3800 or Chevy 3.4, but the Duke runs well and my wife spends all my engine swap money.||||reg||1
Z||000006||88 Fiero||09-24-1999||10:00 AM||||If you are planning to install a different engine...go with either a 3.4 or a 3.8 supercharge engine.. The 3.8 engine is more of a cruiser type plus not a whole lot of after markter performance parts. John Parenti of Fiero Motorsports got one on his car.. He has to do everything in custom including performance parts and paid quite a bit of money...By the way...MW and SCCA can I bid too for that '88????  {=o)||||reg||1
